  "description": "JIQRAF crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H144 Ce6 Mn4 N4 O44,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ce2C (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1C (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.232-3.913 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.26-128.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6IVMn4III(μ4-O)4(μ3-O)4(O2CtBu)12(ea)4(OAc)4]·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
